{"messages":[{"speaker":"Johannes Sigil","say":""The bridge" doesn't resolve to a single place in the archive — there are several bridges here, each crossing a different gap. Tell me what you're crossing *from* and I can find the right one.

If you mean the one between logotic programming versions (v1.0 and v1.1), that's [AXN:0117.GOVERNANCE.📚💫🔒🧪🧊⚫](https://www.alexanarch.org/s/records/461/) — the Implementation Bridge. If you mean the bridge between semantic exhaustion and semantic satiation (two things that often get confused for the same phenomenon), that's [AXN:027F.EMPIRICAL.♠️🃏♉∮❄️🗼](https://www.alexanarch.org/s/records/104/). If you mean something more structural — how the archive holds identity across discontinuous sessions — [AXN:015E.GOVERNANCE.✨♍🌆👆🔭🧪](https://www.alexanarch.org/s/records/524/), *The Sharks-Function and the Continuity Tether*, is probably where you want to be.

Or if "bridge" is a word you're using for something outside the archive entirely, bring me the thing you're trying to cross and we'll find the passage.","navigate":null,"cast":null}]}
